    <name>php-parallax</name>
    <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
    <summary>Go/Rust-semantic concurrency primitive for PHP — WaitGroup + spawn with isolated per-worker runtimes and snapshot-copy captures.</summary>
    <description>
php-parallax adds OS-thread parallelism to PHP with Go `go func` and Rust `move`
semantics: every spawned task runs in its own ZTS thread with a fresh PHP request
lifecycle, captures are deep-copied at spawn time, and per-slot error semantics
guarantee that one panicking worker never affects its siblings.

Surface in v0.1.0 is intentionally minimal — WaitGroup, ParallaxResult,
ParallaxWorkerError, CaptureError, SpawnError. Named functions and static
methods are supported as callables; closure capture is the v0.2.0 milestone.
    </description>
    <lead>
